==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-год.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|[ɡot]|lang=ru}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|orv|ru}} {{term|годъ||time, period|lang=orv}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|gʰedʰ-|to unite, be associated, be suitable|lang=ru}}. Cognates include Ukrainian {{l|uk|годi}} (enough), Bulgarian {{l|bg|годе}} ([[ever]], as in {{l|bg|кой-годе}} = whoever), Czech {{l|cs|hod}}, Polish {{l|pl|gódy}} (feast), Upper Sorbian [[hody]] (Christmas), Lower Sorbian [[gódy]] (Christmas), Latvian {{l|lv|gads}} (year), German {{l|de|Gatte}} (husband) and {{l|de|gätlich}} (convenient), as well as English [[gather]] and [[good]], Dutch {{l|nl|goed}}, and German {{l|de|gut}}. Descendants include Russian {{l|ru|погода}}, {{l|ru|выгода}}, {{l|ru|угода}}, {{l|ru|годный}}, and {{l|ru|годиться}}.

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|tr=god|g=m|sc=Cyrl}}, [[годы]] (gódy) {{p}}, [[года]] (godá) {{p}}

# [[year]]
#:* {{Cyrl|[[в#Russian|в]] [[этот|э́том]] году́}} — ''this year''
#:* {{Cyrl|года́ми}} — ''for years; for years on end''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[девяностый|девяно́стые]] го́ды}} — ''the ’90s''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[учебный|уче́бный]] год}} — ''school year; academic year''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[новый|Но́вый]] год}} — ''New Year’s Day''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[он|Ему́]] [[двадцать один|два́дцать оди́н]] год}} — ''He is 21 years old.''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[он|Ему́]] [[двадцать три|два́дцать три]] го́да}} — ''He is 23 years old.''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[он|Ему́]] [[двадцать пять|два́дцать пять]] [[лето|лет]]}} — ''He is 25 years old.''
#:* {{Cyrl|[[тысяча]] [[девятьсот]] [[девяносто]] [[второй]] год}} (týsjača devjatʹsót devjanósto vtorój god) {{m}} - (year) 1992 (''in words'')
#:* {{Cyrl|[[две]] [[тысяча|тысячи]] [[одиннадцатый]] год}} (dve týsjači odínnadcatyj god) {{m}} - (year) 2011 (''in words'')

====Usage notes====
* Use the appropriate case of '''''год''''' after simple or compound numbers ending in ''[[один]]'' (1), ''[[два]]'' (2), ''[[три]]'' (3), or ''[[четыре]]'' (4), except for 11, 12, 13 and 14 (and 111 - 114, 211 - 214 etc.) - for these and all other numbers, and with [[adverb]]s of quantity (''[[много]]'', ''[[сколько]]'', etc.), use the appropriate case of '''''[[лето]]'''.
